<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barasoain Church</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barasoain Church is a Catholic church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulacan">Bulacan</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. In September 1898 it hosted the Malolos Congress, which drafted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos-constitution">Malolos Constitution</a>, and on 23 January 1899 the First Philippine Republic was inaugurated there with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> as president. It is a national shrine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barasoain-church.jpg" alt="Barasoain Church" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tagaaplaya · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barasoain_Church_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
